\title{Conjunction in Disco}
\date{2026-01-28T20:38:32Z}
\tag{discrete}

\import{discrete-macros}

\p{In Disco, conjunction can be written \code{\verb<<<|/\<<<}, or \tt{and}, or \tt{&&}:
\pre\verb<<<|
Disco> T and F
F
Disco> (1 < 5) && (6 <= 6)
T
Disco> true /\ (99 == 990)
F<<<
}

\p{As before, we can also get Disco to [show us a truth table](002X):
\pre\verb<<<|
Disco> :table /\
F  F  F
F  T  F
T  F  F
T  T  T<<<
The rows are in a different order than the table shown previously, but the order of the rows doesn't really matter.
}
